JMK <jeffrey.m.klopotic@lmco.nospam.com> writes:

>// Global
>char *f1 = "default.str";
>	strcpy (f1, pfix); <-------- 	Program received signal SIGSEGV,

You are trying to overwrite a string constant, which may
reside in read-only memory.  Thus the crash.

You should fix your application to avoid doing that.
As a workaround, you could also use the -fwritable-strings
flag that tell gcc to allow writing to string "constants".

