That's also true for the HighPoint-based ide raid cards. I have installed
many TX2s and HPT-370s in the past, although they all were in x86/linux
boxes. Performance was not bad, you know... The only catch here is I've
been using the modules provided by Promise and HighPoint respectively and
not the ones in the standard linux kernel tree (pdcraid and hptraid that
is), and that iirc none of these two companies provided an alpha version
of their modules. On the other hand, imho a true hardware raid card is
much better than a software raid one, given the smaller (expected)
footprint of the driver and the (much) lower inflicted cpu overhead.

